{
 "nodes": [
  {
   "nodeID": "345",
   "text": "Does the low October 2025 trade deficit mean the tariffs are working?",
   "type": "I",
   "role": "question",
   "toulmin": "framing",
   "oper": "framing",
   "localID": "setser_2026-02-03_october-2025-deficit#Q"
  },
  {
   "nodeID": "346",
   "text": "Tariffs reduce the trade deficit only if their proceeds reduce the budget deficit, acting as a tax hike",
   "type": "I",
   "role": "stated_assumption",
   "toulmin": "warrant",
   "oper": "warrant.prior",
   "localID": "setser_2026-02-03_october-2025-deficit#P1"
  },
  {
   "nodeID": "347",
   "text": "Remove pharmaceuticals and gold to read the underlying deficit",
   "type": "I",
   "role": "stated_assumption",
   "toulmin": "warrant",
   "oper": "warrant.prior",
   "localID": "setser_2026-02-03_october-2025-deficit#P2"
  },
  {
   "nodeID": "348",
   "text": "The trade balance is a macroeconomic savings-investment outcome; inventory swings reverse over time",
   "type": "I",
   "role": "hidden_assumption",
   "toulmin": "warrant",
   "oper": "warrant.prior",
   "localID": "setser_2026-02-03_october-2025-deficit#P3"
  },
  {
   "nodeID": "349",
   "text": "October's drop came entirely from pharmaceuticals and gold; excluding them, October's deficit was slightly bigger than September's; August to October deficits below 2024, but early 2025 far above; imports of autos and household durable goods down; imports of semiconductors and computers up",
   "type": "I",
   "role": "evidence_data",
   "toulmin": "grounds",
   "oper": "grounds",
   "localID": "setser_2026-02-03_october-2025-deficit#E1"
  },
  {
   "nodeID": "350",
   "text": "U.S. trade data; Section 232 semiconductor investigation",
   "type": "I",
   "role": "evidence_source",
   "toulmin": "grounds",
   "oper": "grounds",
   "localID": "setser_2026-02-03_october-2025-deficit#E2"
  },
  {
   "nodeID": "351",
   "text": "Fear of tariffs that never came drove pharmaceutical stockpiling and gold flowing out and back",
   "type": "I",
   "role": "mechanism",
   "toulmin": "warrant",
   "oper": "warrant.mechanism",
   "localID": "setser_2026-02-03_october-2025-deficit#M1"
  },
  {
   "nodeID": "352",
   "text": "Stockpiles built ahead of tariffs temporarily depress imports, and stockpiles run out",
   "type": "I",
   "role": "mechanism",
   "toulmin": "warrant",
   "oper": "warrant.mechanism",
   "localID": "setser_2026-02-03_october-2025-deficit#M2"
  },
  {
   "nodeID": "353",
   "text": "The data center buildout keeps semiconductor and computer imports rising",
   "type": "I",
   "role": "mechanism",
   "toulmin": "warrant",
   "oper": "warrant.mechanism",
   "localID": "setser_2026-02-03_october-2025-deficit#M3"
  },
  {
   "nodeID": "354",
   "text": "Promised refund checks and pressure for more defense spending block a fiscal adjustment",
   "type": "I",
   "role": "mechanism",
   "toulmin": "warrant",
   "oper": "warrant.mechanism",
   "localID": "setser_2026-02-03_october-2025-deficit#M4"
  },
  {
   "nodeID": "355",
   "text": "Tariffs reduce imports in specific categories, but the overall deficit is driven by untariffed goods and stockpile timing",
   "type": "I",
   "role": "intermediate_claim",
   "toulmin": "claim",
   "oper": "claim.step",
   "localID": "setser_2026-02-03_october-2025-deficit#C1"
  },
  {
   "nodeID": "356",
   "text": "No: the low October deficit is not evidence the tariffs work, and a significant fall in the 2025 deficit is unlikely",
   "type": "I",
   "role": "main_claim",
   "toulmin": "claim",
   "oper": "claim.final",
   "localID": "setser_2026-02-03_october-2025-deficit#K"
  },
  {
   "nodeID": "357",
   "text": "Trump's trade team claiming success from smaller deficits than in the same months of 2024",
   "type": "I",
   "role": "opposing_view",
   "toulmin": "rebuttal",
   "oper": "rebuttal",
   "localID": "setser_2026-02-03_october-2025-deficit#X"
  },
  {
   "nodeID": "358",
   "text": "Tariffed categories really are falling; watch whether imports rebound once stockpiles are exhausted",
   "type": "I",
   "role": "caveat",
   "toulmin": "qualifier",
   "oper": "qualifier",
   "localID": "setser_2026-02-03_october-2025-deficit#QF"
  },
  {
   "nodeID": "359",
   "text": "Auto imports fell along with auto sales: weaker demand rather than more U.S. production",
   "type": "I",
   "role": "other_explanation",
   "toulmin": "rebuttal",
   "oper": "rebuttal",
   "localID": "setser_2026-02-03_october-2025-deficit#R1"
  },
